    {
      "title": "Easy Solutions",
      "slug": "easy-solutions",
      "displayOrder": 2,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 7,
        "lessonOrder": 2
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151857740",
              "title": "Stitch Types and Yarn Usage",
              "legacyComponentId": 47,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Compare Stitch patterns",
          "slug": "compare-stitch-patterns",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 72,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><small>Stitches and rows shown are for standard machine <em>(Mid-gauge/bulky)</em></small></blockquote>\r\n<b>Swatch 1:</b><br>\r\n<ol class=”Instruction-list”>\r\n<li>Cast on 60 (30) stitches and knit in plain knitting for 60(30) rows</li>\r\n<li>Bind off loosely</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<b>Swatch 2:</b><br>\r\n<li>Cast on 60 (30) stitches and knit in a tuck stitch knitting for 60(30) rows<br><small>If you don't have an automatic patterning machine (punchcard or electronics)\r\n follow your manual for manually creating a tuck or Pull-up stitch</small></li>\r\n<li>Bind off loosely</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<br>Compare and measure the 2 swatches - notice that both the width and length vary quite a bit.  Simply using a tuck stitch can sometimes solve the problem of not having enough needles to knit a piece.<br>\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/2/not_enough_needles/compare.jpg\">\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 764,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "migrationPending",
              "legacyType": "ImageUpload",
              "notes": [
                "Unmapped legacy component type: ImageUpload"
              ],
              "legacyFields": {
                "ACTION": "stitchPatternPractice",
                "BUTTONLABLE": "Upload Photos of your Practice Swatches<br><small>They will be included in your Course Binder</small>",
                "CHALLENGE_ASSIGNID": "252",
                "CHALLENGE_COMPONENTID": "765",
                "QTY": "2",
                "SUCCESSMESSAGE": "Got it!"
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 765,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Stitch Pattern Practice",
          "slug": "stitch-pattern-practice",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 252,
            "blockType": "Practice"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "If you have a ribber, you can utilize both beds. This is also called \"U\" knitting.<br>\r\nBut remember, on Japanese machines automatic stitch patterning only occurs on the main bed. This solution will produce a wide piece of plain stockinette knitting. <br>You can use a textured or variegated yarn ... or even stripes to jazz up the plain knitting and create a wide knitted piece - get creative!",
              "legacyComponentId": 782,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859462",
              "title": "Half Circular U-Knitting",
              "legacyComponentId": 757,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Half Circular Knitting with the Ribber",
          "slug": "half-circular-knitting-with-the-ribber",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 73,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<b>Practice:</b><br>\r\nIf you have a ribber, following the video and your manual cast on 30 stitches on each bed and set your machine to knit half tubular (U knitting).<br>Once you get in the rhythm, the knitting isn't difficult and the advantage is a wide piece of knitting with no seams.<br>\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/2/not_enough_needles/half1.jpg\">\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 766,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "migrationPending",
              "legacyType": "ImageUpload",
              "notes": [
                "Unmapped legacy component type: ImageUpload"
              ],
