    {
      "title": "Pattern Hacking Practice",
      "slug": "pattern-hacking-practice",
      "displayOrder": 70,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 5,
        "lessonOrder": 70
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<center><img src=\"http://kin.knititnow.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Not_enough_pinterest-300x168.jpg\"></center><br>\r\n<p>Just because a pattern tells us to cast on the entire width of the back of a sweater, doesn't mean we have to do that.  Often with Knit it Now Dynamic Patterns, you will be instructed to cast on more stitches than you have available. (The engine does it's math thing, but doesn't know how many needles you have available.)<br>As shown in the previous \"Not Enough Needles II\" video, we have options for adding seams.</p>\r\n<p>Let's do a little math and explore 5 possibilities.</p>",
              "legacyComponentId": 792,
              "order": 2
            },
